SPARTA (24 Sep 2025)
Running on 1 MPI task(s)
################################################################################
# time-average per-grid custom attributes with fix ave/grid
#
# fix ave/grid has always had complete downstream support for g_name inputs
# (validation, init, accumulation of both vectors and array columns), and the
# docs list it as supported, but its argument parser accepted only c_/f_/v_ so
# every g_ input was rejected as an illegal command.  This exercises the
# now-reachable path for a custom vector and for both columns of a custom
# array, of int and float type.
#
# The custom values are constant in time, so each running average must equal
# the underlying value.  c_direct[k] reduces the custom data directly and
# c_ave[k] reduces the fix ave/grid output; the two must agree.
#
# Notes:
#  - The "comm/sort" option to the "global" command is used to match MPI runs.
#  - The "twopass" option is used to match Kokkos runs.
# The "comm/sort" and "twopass" options should not be used for production runs.
################################################################################

seed	    	    12345
dimension   	    2

global              gridcut 0.0 comm/sort yes

boundary	    or r p

create_box  	    0 10 0 10 -0.5 0.5
Created orthogonal box = (0 0 -0.5) to (10 10 0.5)
create_grid 	    10 10 1
Created 100 child grid cells
  CPU time = 0.000739296 secs
  create/ghost percent = 95.7055 4.29449
balance_grid        rcb cell
Balance grid migrated 0 cells
  CPU time = 8.8396e-05 secs
  reassign/sort/migrate/ghost percent = 81.1801 0.490972 10.1848 8.14403

global		    nrho 1.0 fnum 0.01

species		    air.species N O
mixture		    air N O vstream 100.0 0 0

compute             cid property/grid all id

run                 0
